msgid "System disk handoff for VM{vmid}\n\nImage: {filename}\nHostname: {hostname}\n{network}\n1. Verify sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.\n2. Prepare a powered-off VM with UEFI/OVMF and Secure Boot disabled.\n   Recommended resources: {vcpus} CPUs, {memory} MiB RAM, {disk} GiB disk.\n3. Import QCOW2 into the chosen storage and attach it as virtio0 or scsi0 (VirtIO SCSI).\n   Configure boot from the attached disk and enable QEMU Guest Agent.\n4. {adapters}\n   For a static IP, the connected network must match the listed subnet and gateway.\n5. In the console, verify ip -4 address, ip route and resolvectl status.\n   System: readlink -f /run/current-system; the expected value is in manifest.json.\n\n{identity}\nManual import does not adopt ownership markers required for hypervisor management.\nManage the server through access in its declaration or nixberry update TARGET --ssh root@HOST:PORT --apply.\nSSH access uses keys from the included recipe; password login is disabled.\nThe image supplies the system; the operator manages the host, bridge and firewall.\n"
