#: deployment/exporter.py:147
#, python-brace-format
msgid "System disk handoff for VirtualBox on Linux and Windows\n\nImage: {filename}\nHostname: {hostname}\n{network}\n1. Verify SHA256SUMS before import. On Linux: sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.\n   On Windows, compare Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 '{filename}' with its SHA256SUMS entry.\n2. Create a new Linux (64-bit) VM, skip unattended installation and do not attach an ISO.\n   Resources: {vcpus} CPUs, {memory} MiB RAM. Enable UEFI and leave Secure Boot disabled.\n3. First copy the VDI outside the bundle; attach this existing disk to the SATA controller.\n   The image has {disk} GiB capacity and contains the installed system.\n   For another VM, use VBoxManage clonemedium disk to assign a unique media UUID.\n4. {adapters}\n   For DHCP, use Bridged Adapter with DHCP or NAT.\n   For a static IP, the network must match the listed subnet and gateway.\n5. Boot the VM from disk and verify ip -4 address, ip route and systemctl status virtualbox in its console.\n   The expected system (readlink -f /run/current-system) is in manifest.json.\n\nFor NAT, configure SSH port forwarding in the operator's environment.\n{identity}\nManual import does not adopt ownership markers for automatic hypervisor management.\nManage the server through access in the offline declaration or --ssh root@HOST:PORT.\nSSH accepts recipe keys; password login is disabled.\n"
